      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T08:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we share the chained-SEND builder with `rdma_mlx5_tx_regular()`, similarly to the shared TSO builder? These implementations have already diverged: the regular path skips zero-length fragments, while this path counts each one as a data segment. Consequently, enabling eMPW can consume additional WQEBBs or reject a fragmented packet with `SEGMENT_SIZE_EXCEEDED` when the legacy path would transmit it. A common builder returning the status, final control segment, and WQEBB count would allow each caller to retain its different buffer-ring accounting.",
      "revId": "85d127f91c87ed3c3ba4cf389951815c7e54f6fb",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
